SOC Automation Platform
Prerequisites
Basic Linux command line knowledge
Understanding of log files and their structure
Familiarity with text editors (nano or vi)
Basic understanding of security concepts (threats, alerts)
Learning Objectives
By the end of this lab, you will be able to:

Set up a basic SOC automation workflow on a single Linux machine
Ingest and parse security logs
Detect simulated threats using pattern matching
Generate automated alerts based on detections
Create simple security reports
Environment Setup
You will use the bare-metal Linux machine provided by Al Nafi. All tools will be installed during this lab.

Install Required Tools
# Update package manager
sudo apt update

# Install Python3 and pip (if not already installed)
sudo apt install -y python3 python3-pip

# Install required Python libraries
pip3 install watchdog
Create Working Directory
# Create lab directory structure
mkdir -p ~/soc-lab/{logs,scripts,alerts,reports}
cd ~/soc-lab
