Troubleshooting Tips
Issue: No logs generated

Check if log_generator.py is running: ps aux | grep log_generator
Verify write permissions: ls -la logs/
Check for Python errors in the script
Issue: No threats detected

Ensure log file has suspicious events: grep -i "failed\|scan\|unusual" logs/security.log
Verify regex patterns match log format
Check if detector script is running
Issue: Empty report

Confirm alerts file exists and has content: cat alerts/threats.txt
Check file paths in report_generator.py
Verify parsing logic handles alert format correctly
Conclusion
Congratulations! You have successfully built a basic SOC automation platform that:

Ingests logs: Generated and collected security event logs
Detects threats: Identified suspicious patterns using signature-based detection
Generates alerts: Created real-time alerts for detected threats
Produces reports: Automated security reporting with statistics
This workflow demonstrates the core components of Security Operations Centers used by organizations worldwide. In production environments, these systems scale to handle millions of events per day, integrate with SIEM platforms, and use machine learning for advanced threat detection.

Key Takeaways:

Log monitoring is essential for security visibility
Pattern matching enables automated threat detection
Automation reduces response time to security incidents
Reports help security teams prioritize and track threats
